 all avoidable. Just watch every bend, it really picks up speed in the\n\nturns and thats where the wood is. One bridge has a river wide strainer. You'll see it coming, it\n\nwill be the highest bridge you will come to up to that point. Get out and portage on river right.\n\nThe left isn't fun. (I learned the hard way). There are no gauges nearby. Chances are if the\n\nCatskill Creek is running then this creek is also  - Bill S\n\n**Capital Region Area Reaches**\n\n[Basic Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1242/) [Batten Kill](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1245/) [Claverack Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10617/)\n\n[Cobleskill Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1286/) [Fox Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1307/) [Hannacrois Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1318/)\n\n[Hoosic](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1320/) [Hudson (Lock 2)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10624/) [Kinderhook Creek  (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10619/)\n\n[Kinderhook Creek  (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10620/) [Kinderhook Creek  (3.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1333/) [Kline Kill](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10557/)\n\n[Normans Kill (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10871/) [Normans Kill (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10870/) [North Chuctanunda Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10884/)\n\n[Mohawk (Upper Cohoes Wave)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1347/) [Mohawk (Cohoes Wave)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3013/) [Poesten Kill (0.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/c